        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Every NAD address point of the current release, read from the Deflate64 CSV inside TXT.zip in file order (rows are grouped by state and county on disk, not sorted by OID_). Each page reads only the compressed byte range it needs: the cursor carries the release blob id, a Deflate64 block boundary and the 64 KiB of text before it. When the release is replaced mid-run the call fails with invalid_input and issue code publication_changed instead of mixing releases. Records carry all 60 columns plus normalized address, place and coordinate fields.\n\nThe response contains the tool result directly.\n\nThe provider identifies `records` as the primary payload key.\n\n| Documented field | Provider type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `add_auth` | string |  |\n| `addr_class` | string |  |\n| `addr_type` | string |  |\n| `address` | string | AddNo_Full and StNam_Full joined with a space. |\n| `attributes` | object | All 60 TXT columns under their source names, trimmed strings; null for an empty cell. |\n| `county` | string |  |\n| `date_updated` | string | YYYY-MM-DD from DateUpdate (the raw value is in attributes). |\n| `latitude` | number | Latitude parsed as a number; null as for longitude. |\n| `longitude` | number | Longitude parsed as a number; null for an empty cell or (with an unparsed_coordinates warning) an unparseable one. |\n| `nad_source` | string |  |\n| `oid` | number | OID_ column. Unique within a release, not in file order, and not stable across releases. |\n| `placement` | string |  |\n| `post_city` | string |  |\n| `publication_id` | string | files:<release>:<TXT blobId>, the same id source_status returns. |\n| `retrieved_at` | string |  |\n| `row` | number | 1-based data row in the TXT member, after the header. |\n| `source_record_id` | string | UUID column, lowercased without braces when it is a GUID, else as published. Null (with a missing_uuid warning) for an empty cell. |\n| `source_url` | string | TXT.zip download URL the row was read from. |\n| `state` | string |  |\n| `zip_code` | string |  |\n\n\nThese are the provider's documented fields. Field requiredness, nullability and nested object structures are specified only where the descriptions explicitly say so.",
