                      "license": "Published data made available as a part of the NAD is provided as a public service to enhance open government, transparency, and accountability. The NAD is a compilation of data provided by state, local, and tribal governments and is made available \"as is.\" Although the NAD is open data, it is not intended for use as a mailing list and is subject to individual state statutes that prohibit its use as a mailing list. The NAD is a work of the federal government and as such is not subject to copyright protection in accordance with 17 U.S.C. § 105. It is available for re-use without limitation or restriction.",
                      "observed_at_ms": 1792889963824,
                      "publication_id": "files:r24:596a301b-d548-4589-8c63-6b6a8dc34f30",
                      "release": {
                        "compiled_on": "2026-09-30",
                        "description": "The Address Points from National Address Database dataset was compiled on September 30, 2026 by the US Department of Transportation. The National Address Database (NAD) is a spatial database containing address data, point location coordinates, jurisdictions, record-level metadata and other supporting data for addressable locations including structures, some sub-units within those structures, and landmarks as included in the aggregated datasets from providers included therein.\n\nTechnical Note: Record Ordering and Object IDs\nPlease Note: The records in this flat text file are structured in their optimized physical database order, rather than numerical sequence by OID_ (Object ID). Because the National Address Database leverages highly efficient spatial indexing and bit-packing compression algorithms before export, geographically clustered records (such as specific states or counties) are grouped together on disk.\n\nAll OID_ values remain perfectly unique across the entire dataset, but they will appear out of chronological order when reading the file sequentially. If your integration workflow requires a strict numerical sequence, you can safely sort the dataset by the OID_ column upon ingestion.",
                        "id": "r24",
